Subject: [PATCH] Seal what was measured: a failed blob read is no longer
 sealed as <absent>

MEASURED ON THIS BOX 2026-09-24. release_identity refused NEW risk with "running the
sealed commit 6bd53e64c325; money path drifted on disk: [gateway.py, decision_core.py,
sizing.py, scalp_exec.py, netting.py, execution_policy.py, ...]" and the money path had
not drifted by a byte: all 22 files hashed identical to `git show <code_sha>:<path>`,
git porcelain was clean on them, and code_sha equalled HEAD -- so the commit comparison
passed and every investigation stopped there. 1,222 of the last 1,266 decisions were
release_identity_refused; 42 were placed. The desk has not placed since 05:56Z.

THE CAUSE. `_read` returned None for two different facts -- "git says this path is not
in that commit" and "git would not answer" -- and `hash_paths` hashed the sentinel
`<absent>` for both. Measured: 19 of the 22 money-path digests in RELEASE.json were
exactly sha256(path + b"<absent>")[:16], while `git ls-tree` shows all 22 ARE in the
tree at the sealed commit. The seal had recorded present files as absent and written it
as a signed fact. The same flap hit the same record three more ways: config_hash came
out half-absent, allocator_hash came out correct, and canon_sha256 / immutable_manifest
came out NULL for two files that are in the tree -- nulls that read as "there wasn't
one" and meant "nobody could look" (L1.28a, WS-005).

THE FIX, at the cause and without weakening the rail.
  * `_Blobs` asks `git ls-tree` which kind of None it has. A path IN the tree that will
    not read raises SealReadError; a path genuinely not in the tree still hashes to the
    sentinel, so a legitimately untracked entry seals exactly as before.
  * One cached reader per `_describe`, so a record cannot disagree with itself the way
    heat_policy.py did (absent in config_hash, present in allocator_hash, same record).
  * `manifest_describes_commit()` re-derives the manifest from the commit it names,
    through a reader of its own, and `seal()` runs it BEFORE writing. A manifest that
    does not describe its own sha is never written: the previous honest record stands.
    The sha and the hashes now advance together or neither does.
  * `money_path_absent` is recorded, so absence is legible instead of hidden in a digest.
  * `git show` timeout 10s -> 30s: a short timeout only buys a faster wrong answer, and
    the wrong answer now raises instead of being sealed.
  * release_identity says which of the two it found, so a recurrence costs one log line
    rather than a day.

NOT DONE, deliberately: the money-path stage is not removed, the allowlist is not
widened, today's hashes are not stamped over the manifest, and no identity is forged. A
real on-disk drift still refuses -- pinned by test_a_real_on_disk_drift_still_refuses.

Gates on this box: ruff clean, mypy clean, pytest --co clean, 33/33 green across
test_seal_manifest_is_a_measurement (new, 10), test_release_seal (15) and
test_desk_root_state_files (8). The two failures in test_release_identity.py
(test_smoke_release_passes_on_a_sealed_signed_tree, test_a_crlf_checkout_is_not_drift,
both at line 296) were verified PRE-EXISTING: identical failure with git HEAD's versions
of both files restored.

