+    `seal()` runs this BEFORE it writes, against a reader of its own, so the check is an
+    independent re-derivation rather than a restatement of the dict it just built. A manifest that
+    does not describe its own sha is never written at all: the previous, honest record stands, and
+    the desk gets a red rail telling the truth instead of a green one that is not.
+
+    Raises SealReadError when git cannot answer. Unmeasured is not a pass.
+    """
